      "low_moderate_boundary": 4.2982,
      "moderate_high_boundary": 5.9275,
      "derivation": "training-set terciles (P33.33, P66.67)",
      "training_samples": 3150,
      "training_source": "experiments/distortion_analysis/distortion_metrics.csv"
    },
    "threshold_justification": "Thresholds are the global P33.33 and P66.67 of mean displacement magnitude across 3,150 training samples (1,050 per distortion type). Derived from training data only.",
    "notes": [
      "The continuous severity score (mean displacement) is the primary metric. Categorical labels are a convenience derived from training-set terciles.",
      "Categorical severity labels correlate strongly with distortion type: local distortions are predominantly Low severity, elastic is predominantly High, bending spans all three.",
      "Severity does not imply rectification success. Higher severity = larger predicted displacement that DDRNet must correct."
    ]
